   "cite": "probabilities-to-q",
   "prompt": "<p>A system has two states, of energy 0 and $\\varepsilon$, at a temperature where $k\\kT = \\varepsilon$. Find $\\kSent/k$ from $\\kSent = -k\\sum_j p_j\\ln p_j$, and check it against $\\kSent = \\kU/\\kT + k\\ln \\kQsys$.</p>",
   "answer": {
    "type": "number",
    "value": 0.582,
    "generated_by": "ai",
    "hint": "With $\\beta\\varepsilon = 1$, $Q = 1 + e^{-1}$.",
    "solution": "<p>$\\kQsys = 1 + e^{-1} = 1.368$, so $p_0 = 1/1.368 = 0.731$ and $p_1 = e^{-1}/1.368 = 0.269$. Then $\\kSent/k = -(0.731\\ln 0.731 + 0.269\\ln 0.269) = 0.229 + 0.353 = 0.582$. Check: $\\kU = p_1\\varepsilon = 0.269\\,\\varepsilon$, so $\\kU/k\\kT = 0.269$, and $\\ln \\kQsys = 0.313$; their sum is 0.582, the same.</p>"
   }
  }
 ],
